{
 "a_question_this_raises_and_does_not_answer": {
  "what": "the 8-K/A amends the same January event the original 8-K reported - same report date - so C01 counts one leadership change twice.",
  "what_it_is": "a question about whether the definition answers the metric's own name. That is a correctness standard, not an implementation choice, and the acceptance register says explicitly that it does not establish it.",
  "why_it_is_not_a_defect_here": "the approved definition for C01 is '来源：8-K Item 5.02。输出事件清单：date、accession、item code、brief', which specifies an event list keyed by accession. One entry per filing carrying the item is what it asks for."
 },
 "both_window_bases": "every accepted count is the same under the filing date and the report date, so it does not depend on which reading of the window is taken.",
